ry hard here  to get the pay rise that our members  deserve  well yes you say they're making record  profits royal mail says your proposals  would cost a billion pounds well it's  losing almost a million pounds a day  they say that  their business is suffering there are  fewer coveted tests being delivered for  example there are fewer people shopping  online post pandemic  and there's a steeply declining letter  market and they simply have to be able  to compete with with some of their  competitors so  that's reasonable isn't it  anna anna listen i i wish you could get  royal mal  to debate these issues and the statement  that you've just read out  because we would take that debate  anywhere any place any time and to point  out that it's a total fabrication of the  truth of what's going on in this company  and these people are being less than  honest with you less than honest with  their customers and and you know it's  just not on i mean they made record  profits  they have said that their bonuses  were achieved because they hit all of  their financial targets and yes there  are some issues we understand that  we will never face away from change it's  our union that wants to get on and do  the right change that protects the  company for the future but the company  has stood those talks we've got a second  ballot on change because they've walked  away from the agreement that we reached  with them and something that i've got to  raise today  that we wrote to the company about a  couple of days back we really do believe  that sitting behind this dispute the  motives for this company is that they  are involved at the moment in secret  discussions um on a takeover of this  company i'm bringing in one of these  the same type of scenario private equity  investment group in this case a company  called visa from luxembourg  and they are going to asset strip this  company they're going to abandon the  universal service and they want to turn  royal mail to make more profits for  themselves and the shareholders into  another gig economy employer and we are  not going to accept that  okay well we will certainly put that to  the company um in the meantime royal  mail will say that you've rejected a  deal you say it's two percent they say  it's 5.5 because they say that an extra  3.5 percent is is subject to agreement  on a series of changes so why are you  rejecting that  well that's pie in the sky and i'm sorry  to go back to the same thing it's simply  not true that was that offer as you call  it was put to our members directly by  the company uh before our members even  voted in the numbers that i just  described earlier on it is pie in the  sky the two percent was imposed two  percent of that is supposedly against a  productivity scheme that doesn't exist  and nobody in the company can sit in  front of anybody in the union and  explain what it is our members have got  to do to earn that two percent and the  other 1.5 of that is against a leveling  down agenda one of these piano style  leveling down agendas um which will  destroy the post office as we know it  royal mail as we know it and we're not  going to accept it i'm sorry to say  it's completely untrue what they're  saying to you and our members know that  postal workers would not be voting in  the numbers that they're voting in if  any of what you said was true but by the  way 5.5  even if it was there is not enough  against inflation and against the  horrendous energy bills that our members  and millions of other people in this  country are going to be facing  dave water we're likely to see a general  strike in this country do you think  would you back one if there was one  called  look i'm not here to talk about a  general strike what i will say to you  is that you know i think people across  the uk  every worker counts every worker's in  the same position  and yes i think we should be looking at  cold and hated action we should be  looking to raise  issues around the way that 